figure by an `int8` key is answered from a byte table	matrix cells set_anti_1000 of bench/steps/join_matrix.py at 1,000,000 and 10,000,000 rows (a fact of those rows, a dimension of half as many, 20 sets of 1,000 members; sift_col index on the fact and the dimension; arms native, off, on; user instructions of all processes by perf stat, rows equal by md5); the bench case semi_lut_bigint holds the 1,000,000-row shape at bench scale
figure is read from the cache of an earlier statement as classes of its keys	measurement of the reproducer of the shared-dimension notes (a table of 1,000,000 rows, a parent of 100,000 keys with 60 levels and 7 values of a second column, one backend by perf stat, instructions per execution as (7 runs - 3 runs) / 4, answers equal to the normal plan): the tip before this change 245.7 and 475.0 M, after 104.5 and 261.8 M; the bench case lookup_dense_kept holds the shape at bench scale
commit e68ea604c	a ceiling on the rows of a segment of a key_cut build, not a speed: test/sql/col_key_cut_segment_cap.sql builds 3.2 million rows at the real 128-segment directory under an array limit and holds the bound; no statement of the registry reads the build arrays
commit 10ce9e0e6	a plan choice between the walk of the order array and the units for a list page under a second test (2.68 to 1.81 and 3.63 to 1.96 million instructions on 25,000 rows to a group); the registry has no list page under a second filter on a key_order group, test/sql/col_topn_walk_price.sql pins the choice on 1,000,000 rows
figure a list page of one group under a test of another column	measurement of 16 list pages (1,000,000 rows, groups of 25,000 and 2,500 rows, a test passed by 50, 10, 2 and 0.5% of the rows, with and without the primary key ending the order): the walk and the units counted by instructions of one backend, the default equal to the cheaper in all 16; test/sql/col_topn_walk_price.sql pins the choice
commit 783b4d09f	a ceiling on the memory of a key_cut build, not a speed: test/sql/col_key_cut_segment_cap.sql builds 3.2 million rows, a third of them one value, under an array limit at the real 128-segment directory, and test/sql/col_key_cut_hot_value.sql holds the rule; no statement of the registry reads the build arrays
commit ae68778a0	which step of a rewrite chooses the options of a sift_col index again from the data, not a speed: test/sql/col_key_cut_redecide.sql (worker off) and col_key_cut_redecide_async.sql (worker on) hold the choice; no statement of the registry rewrites a churned index
figure are columns of its lookup table, which are computed once for each row	measurement of a fact table of 1,000,000 and of 10,000,000 rows (id, key, value) joined to a parent of 100,000 and 1,000,000 unique int4 keys with three attributes of 7, 40 and 1,000 values (7,000 tuples), sift_col indexes on both; user instructions of all processes by perf stat, (7 runs - 3 runs) / 4 executions in one backend, release library, answers equal to the normal plan by md5): normal plan 1,846 ms and 15,748 M, scan 124 ms and 2,324 M at 10,000,000 rows; 325 ms and 1,789 M against 22 ms and 247 M at 1,000,000; the bench case lookup_dense_tests holds the shape at bench scale
figure an `EXISTS` or `NOT EXISTS` over a `sift_table` (a table of another access method) is no longer taken	a correction of a price so the normal plan is kept, not a speed: test/sql/agg_probe_table_am.sql pins the plans, the figures are one measurement of a 1,000,000-row sift_table with the probe forced and not
figure a join to a table kept as classes of its keys answered wrongly	a wrong answer fixed, not a speed: agg_lookup_tests shapes 10 to 14 compare the rows with the normal plan
figure a join to a table kept as classes of its keys resolves the rows of a chunk in one loop	measured with perf stat in the commit (cycles and instructions of 20 runs, 1,000,000 rows x 100,000 keys); test/sql/agg_lookup_tests.sql pins the answers, lookup_dense_kept the plan
figure the `float4`, `float8` and `time` columns of a joined table are read from the leaves	measured with perf stat in the commit (instructions per row of the load, 100,000-row table); test/sql/agg_lookup_leaf_types.sql pins the values and the leaf read
figure `count(x)` of a column of a joined table keeps a flag	measured with perf stat in the commit (instructions and cycles of the cold run, min of five); test/sql/agg_join_count_flag.sql pins the answers and the prices
figure the classes of a dense table of more than 524,288 keys are asked for 64 keys ahead	measured in the commit (EXPLAIN ANALYZE, minimum of five, one backend); test/sql/agg_lookup_dense_far.sql pins the answers on such a table
figure a lookup table that repeats a key is priced as rows	measured in the commit (EXPLAIN ANALYZE, minimum of three, one backend); test/sql/agg_join_repeated_key_price.sql pins the price of a repeated key against a unique one
figure a joined table's `uuid`, `interval`, `bytea`, `inet` and `numeric` of more than 18 digits columns	measured in the commit (EXPLAIN ANALYZE, minimum of four, one backend, lookup caches off); test/sql/agg_lookup_wide_classes.sql pins the answers and that the table is read as classes
figure a parallel aggregate whose scan joins one table by a plain integer, date or timestamp key splits the rows of the scan by that key	measured with perf stat on the processes of one cluster (instructions of the leader and the workers, paired and alternating runs) on 5,000,000 children of 100,000 parents by the join-matrix lane's script, not by a bench case: a case of that size is not in the quick tier and the plan and the rows are pinned by the test agg_par_join_split
figure are looked up by their codes with one gather of four values on AVX2 and AVX-512	measured with perf stat on one backend (user instructions, minimum of 5) on a table of 5,000,000 rows by the join-matrix lane's script, not by a bench case; the answers are pinned by the test agg_dict_values_gather and the kernels by col_kernels_simd
figure are added tuple by tuple for the integer, date, timestamp and `float8` columns	measured with perf stat on one backend (user instructions and wall time, minimum of three) on 5,000,000 children of 250,000 parents by the join-matrix lane's script, not by a bench case; the answers are pinned by the test agg_mapped_direct_values
figure a lookup table that another lookup of the scan keeps rows of	measured with the join matrix cell snowflake_filter_tail at 1,000,000 rows by sift.explain_why (the prices) and EXPLAIN ANALYZE (the rows read); the price against the price over every tenant is pinned by the test agg_join_chain_load_price
